Fillets: an OnSame end where the rounding runs on into an earlier rounding
of its radius, its end section lying in that rounding's tube (mitcad#236).

A wall's foot is rounded with the radius of an earlier rounding round the
wall's end: that rounding's tube leaves the wall's side tangentially (its
spine curving away from the side's foot), its floor contact crossing the
wall's plane at the vertex where the new rounding's spine ends, and the
earlier rounding was cut back to the wall's plane there. At that OnSame
end the earlier rounding is the face at the end; the new blend's section
where its spine is tangent to the earlier rounding's lies in that tube, the
two surfaces tangent along it, and the prolonged edge is the earlier
rounding's tangent contact with the floor. The corner intersected the
opposite contact with the face at the end, which it only touches ("OneCorner
: bouchon non ecrit" where no point was found), and then the blend with that
face, tangent to it all along the section ("OneCorner : echec calcul
intersection"); a stored body's earlier rounding, a B-spline whose contact
edge ends at the vertex, also left the prolonged edge without a curve past
the vertex.

ChFi3d_Builder::PerformOneCorner, at an OnSame end:
- where the opposite contact does not cross the face at the end, takes the
  point where it touches the face's surface within the tolerance, the blend
  tangent to the face there (ChFi3d_ContactTouchesEndFace);
- where the blend's end section lies in the face's surface, tangent to it
  along the section, caps the blend with that section, as an end section
  lying in a face at the end already is (0410);
- where the prolonged edge's own curve ends at the vertex but the edge runs
  along an iso of the face's surface, prolongs it along that iso
  (ChFi3d_ProlongTangentEdgeAlongIso, as ChFi3d_ProlongTangentEdge does with
  the edge's curve where that goes on past the vertex).
The face at the end grows up to the section, as the bodies stored in the
files have it; other ends are unchanged.
